---
description: Restart the dev stack only through make dev-restart; ask first for anything else.
alwaysApply: true
---

After a server-code change, `tsx watch` in the dev stack reloads on its own. When a restart is
still needed, restart the dev stack yourself — but ONLY through `make dev-restart`, or a process
you started yourself in this session.

- `make dev-restart` fetches the dev stack's secrets from Infisical and restarts the app, the
  Companion and both gates. If it fails, stop and ask the user; never `docker restart` or
  `docker exec` into a container to restart or start a server.
- Never start a second server by hand (in `make dev-shell` or anywhere): the server refuses a
  data directory another server holds, and the host refuses to boot it at all.
- Any other process or container — an unidentified listener on `:8787`, anything outside the
  `autologger-dev` project — ask the user first; never restart or kill it yourself.
- Dev runs as a single process on `:8787` inside the dev stack; there is no host dev process and
  no separate `:5173` frontend dev server to manage.
- Reference the Makefile targets (`make help`) rather than reconstructing or duplicating a
  command line here.
